export default [{"s":1.1,"e":2.65,"t":"Episode one."},{"s":2.7,"e":4.74,"t":"Where to start reading X-Men..."},{"s":4.82,"e":6.58,"t":"without losing your mind."},{"s":6.996,"e":12.546,"t":"A few years ago, I walked into Graham Crackers Comics in Chicago, as a grown adult,"},{"s":12.596,"e":16.626,"t":"and asked the guy behind the counter the most embarrassing question you can ask in a"},{"s":16.676,"e":17.916,"t":"comic shop."},{"s":19.556,"e":21.826,"t":"Where do I start with X-Men?"},{"s":21.876,"e":25.346,"t":"Because X-Men is 60 years of comics."},{"s":25.396,"e":27.906,"t":"A dozen books with X-Men in the title."},{"s":27.956,"e":31.196,"t":"And reading orders online that look like tax forms."},{"s":31.396,"e":33.186,"t":"He didn't hand me a reading order."},{"s":33.236,"e":35.106,"t":"He handed me one book."},{"s":35.156,"e":36.396,"t":"And it worked."},{"s":36.742,"e":38.692,"t":"So that's what this video is."},{"s":38.742,"e":40.092,"t":"Not a reading order."},{"s":40.142,"e":42.258,"t":"Five books. One shelf."},{"s":42.308,"e":43.662,"t":"Let's go."},{"s":44.101,"e":45.211,"t":"Quick background."},{"s":45.261,"e":50.851,"t":"I was eight years old, growing up in Chicagoland, in 1992, when X-Men: The Animated"},{"s":50.901,"e":52.251,"t":"Series came on..."},{"s":52.301,"e":54.611,"t":"and flipped a switch in my brain."},{"s":54.661,"e":59.661,"t":"That theme song still lives rent free, and it gets me pumped every single time."},{"s":60.08,"e":62.67,"t":"My best friend is the one who got us all into it."},{"s":62.72,"e":65.55,"t":"The cartoon, the comics, all of it."},{"s":65.6,"e":67.32,"t":"So he got first pick..."},{"s":67.4,"e":69.15,"t":"and he picked Gambit."},{"s":69.2,"e":73.55,"t":"Obviously. Gambit and Wolverine were the coolest guys on the show."},{"s":73.6,"e":77.95,"t":"And Gambit had the trench coat, the glowing cards, and an accent none of us could"},{"s":78,"e":79.16,"t":"understand."},{"s":79.32,"e":82.95,"t":"He also decided the girl everybody in class had a crush on..."},{"s":83,"e":84.28,"t":"was Rogue."},{"s":85.28,"e":86.36,"t":"Kids."},{"s":86.796,"e":88.586,"t":"I got Colossus."},{"s":88.636,"e":90.346,"t":"And I felt cheated."},{"s":90.396,"e":95.466,"t":"Big Russian guy, turns into steel, says about four words an episode..."},{"s":95.516,"e":96.986,"t":"but he was mine."},{"s":97.036,"e":98.346,"t":"So I stuck with him."},{"s":98.396,"e":102.106,"t":"And somewhere along the way, I actually started to care about him."},{"s":102.156,"e":103.906,"t":"Strongest guy in the room..."},{"s":103.956,"e":106.036,"t":"and he'd rather be home painting."},{"s":106.459,"e":109.129,"t":"I don't think I'm the only one this happened to."},{"s":109.179,"e":111.369,"t":"A lot of us didn't pick our X-Man."},{"s":111.419,"e":114.729,"t":"We got handed one, and then we got attached."},{"s":114.779,"e":116.569,"t":"That's how I got into X-Men."},{"s":116.619,"e":118.169,"t":"Not through a reading order."},{"s":118.219,"e":119.699,"t":"Through a character."},{"s":119.899,"e":120.889,"t":"Hold on to that."},{"s":120.939,"e":122.899,"t":"I'm gonna come back to it in a minute."},{"s":123.248,"e":125.998,"t":"The obvious move is to start at the beginning."},{"s":126.048,"e":127.678,"t":"X-Men number one."},{"s":127.728,"e":131.038,"t":"1963. It matters historically."},{"s":131.088,"e":132.958,"t":"Stan Lee and Jack Kirby."},{"s":133.008,"e":134.478,"t":"The original five."},{"s":134.528,"e":136.558,"t":"Magneto's first appearance."},{"s":136.608,"e":139.518,"t":"Honestly? It feels like a different team."},{"s":139.568,"e":142.878,"t":"But it's good background, and it matters more than you'd think once we get to"},{"s":142.928,"e":145.288,"t":"Hickman. Hold that thought, too."},{"s":145.706,"e":149.376,"t":"But historically important and a good first read..."},{"s":149.426,"e":151.176,"t":"are not the same thing."},{"s":151.226,"e":154.336,"t":"The storytelling has changed a lot in 60 years."},{"s":154.386,"e":157.426,"t":"And you don't need to do homework to enjoy this stuff."},{"s":157.506,"e":159.696,"t":"So treat it like a tasting menu."},{"s":159.746,"e":161.976,"t":"Five stories, from different eras."},{"s":162.026,"e":163.976,"t":"If one grabs you, follow it."},{"s":164.026,"e":165.976,"t":"If one doesn't, skip it."},{"s":166.026,"e":167.506,"t":"Nobody's checking."},{"s":167.85,"e":170.92,"t":"Number one. The Dark Phoenix Saga."},{"s":170.97,"e":174.52,"t":"Uncanny X-Men 129 through 137."},{"s":174.57,"e":178.04,"t":"1980. Chris Claremont and John Byrne."},{"s":178.09,"e":180.92,"t":"If you only read one X-Men story..."},{"s":180.97,"e":182.68,"t":"it's probably this one."},{"s":182.73,"e":184.68,"t":"It's the team at their peak."},{"s":184.73,"e":188.21,"t":"And it's where a lot of what you know about the X-Men comes from."},{"s":188.558,"e":193.068,"t":"Issue 129 alone introduces Kitty Pryde and Emma Frost."},{"s":193.118,"e":195.228,"t":"130 gives you Dazzler..."},{"s":195.278,"e":197.308,"t":"who's a disco superhero."},{"s":197.358,"e":199.468,"t":"And it's not as corny as it sounds."},{"s":199.518,"e":202.028,"t":"But the real story is Jean Grey."},{"s":202.078,"e":204.108,"t":"She's gained cosmic power."},{"s":204.158,"e":206.428,"t":"The Hellfire Club messes with her head."},{"s":206.478,"e":208.918,"t":"And it goes about as well as you'd expect."},{"s":209.265,"e":214.055,"t":"What makes it hold up is that it's not just a big fight, like Secret Wars."},{"s":214.105,"e":217.465,"t":"It's a team, trying to save a friend from herself."},{"s":217.545,"e":218.745,"t":"And then..."},{"s":219.105,"e":222.308,"t":"137. I'm not gonna spoil it for you."},{"s":222.358,"e":226.905,"t":"I'll just say it's one of the most famous endings in comics, for a reason."},{"s":227.334,"e":231.444,"t":"I'd been through the Phoenix story a bunch of times before I ever read the actual"},{"s":231.494,"e":236.244,"t":"book. The cartoon did it, and honestly, did it really well."},{"s":236.294,"e":238.364,"t":"The movies have tried it twice..."},{"s":238.414,"e":241.044,"t":"and I'm still waiting for one to get it right."},{"s":241.094,"e":242.324,"t":"But it didn't matter."},{"s":242.374,"e":246.884,"t":"Even knowing how it ends, the trade paperback is still the best way to experience"},{"s":246.934,"e":248.884,"t":"it. Team dynamics."},{"s":248.934,"e":250.564,"t":"Real consequences."},{"s":250.614,"e":254.804,"t":"And a character arc that people are still adapting 40 years later."},{"s":254.854,"e":256.564,"t":"If you start anywhere..."},{"s":256.614,"e":257.694,"t":"start here."},{"s":258.125,"e":260.955,"t":"Number two. Days of Future Past."},{"s":261.005,"e":264.325,"t":"Uncanny X-Men 141 and 142."},{"s":264.525,"e":265.515,"t":"Short and sweet."},{"s":265.565,"e":267.915,"t":"Two issues. That covers the whole pitch."},{"s":267.965,"e":273.035,"t":"A future where the Sentinels won, and most of the X-Men are dead, or in camps."},{"s":273.085,"e":276.635,"t":"Kitty's mind gets sent back to the present to stop it from happening."},{"s":276.685,"e":278.555,"t":"It's short. It's dark."},{"s":278.605,"e":282.555,"t":"And it's the blueprint for every stop-the-bad-future story the X-Men have done"},{"s":282.605,"e":284.915,"t":"since. Including the movie..."},{"s":284.965,"e":287.925,"t":"and the cartoon episode you probably saw first."},{"s":288.341,"e":289.491,"t":"Number three."},{"s":289.541,"e":291.331,"t":"X-Cutioner's Song."},{"s":291.381,"e":293.971,"t":"This one's for the kids who grew up on the cartoon."},{"s":294.021,"e":298.931,"t":"'92 into'93. A crossover across four X-books."},{"s":298.981,"e":303.971,"t":"Professor X gets shot, Cable's the main suspect, and it turns into a whole mess with"},{"s":304.021,"e":305.704,"t":"Stryfe and Apocalypse."},{"s":305.754,"e":308.931,"t":"It is the most'90s thing you will ever read."},{"s":308.981,"e":310.371,"t":"Everybody's squinting."},{"s":310.421,"e":312.024,"t":"Everybody has pouches."},{"s":312.074,"e":313.411,"t":"It's pretty rad."},{"s":313.461,"e":317.331,"t":"If the cartoon is your X-Men, this is the comic that feels like it."},{"s":317.381,"e":318.411,"t":"Fair warning..."},{"s":318.461,"e":323.371,"t":"it is messy. It jumps across four different books, so grab the trade paperback."},{"s":323.421,"e":325.421,"t":"Puts everything in order for you."},{"s":325.767,"e":329.317,"t":"Number four. God Loves, Man Kills."},{"s":329.367,"e":330.677,"t":"1982."},{"s":330.727,"e":333.077,"t":"Chris Claremont and Brent Anderson."},{"s":333.127,"e":334.997,"t":"A standalone graphic novel."},{"s":335.047,"e":336.517,"t":"No continuity homework."},{"s":336.567,"e":339.237,"t":"You pick it up, you read it, you're done."},{"s":339.287,"e":344.037,"t":"A preacher named William Stryker starts a crusade against mutants, and the X-Men end"},{"s":344.087,"e":346.357,"t":"up working with Magneto to stop him."},{"s":346.407,"e":350.437,"t":"This is the X-Men at their most direct about what they've always been about."},{"s":350.487,"e":352.277,"t":"Fear. Prejudice."},{"s":352.327,"e":354.597,"t":"People being hated for what they are."},{"s":354.647,"e":358.597,"t":"It's also the backbone of the second X-Men movie, if that's your entry point."},{"s":358.647,"e":363.327,"t":"It's heavy. But it's the one that shows you why these stories still matter."},{"s":363.768,"e":366.198,"t":"Number five. House of M."},{"s":366.248,"e":371.638,"t":"2005. The legendary Brian Michael Bendis, and Olivier Coipel."},{"s":371.688,"e":374.398,"t":"This is the book the guy at Graham Crackers handed me."},{"s":374.448,"e":376.998,"t":"The Scarlet Witch rewrites reality."},{"s":377.048,"e":380.368,"t":"Everybody wakes up in a world where they got what they wanted..."},{"s":380.528,"e":383.638,"t":"and a few of them start to realize something's wrong."},{"s":383.688,"e":388.718,"t":"It's an event book, so it's big, and loud, and it touches the Avengers too."},{"s":388.768,"e":393.118,"t":"But it reads clean, and it was the perfect way back in for me as a young adult."},{"s":393.168,"e":396.278,"t":"And the ending changed the X-Men for about a decade."},{"s":396.328,"e":399.328,"t":"Three words. You'll know them when you see them."},{"s":399.757,"e":403.947,"t":"Once you've got a few of these under your belt, then read House of X and Powers of"},{"s":403.997,"e":404.837,"t":"X."},{"s":405.117,"e":407.867,"t":"2019. Jonathan Hickman."},{"s":407.917,"e":412.187,"t":"It's 12 issues that flip decades of X-Men history on its head."},{"s":412.237,"e":414.107,"t":"Remember X-Men number one?"},{"s":414.157,"e":418.307,"t":"This is where Xavier's choices, going all the way back to the beginning, start"},{"s":418.357,"e":419.467,"t":"catching up with him."},{"s":419.517,"e":420.907,"t":"It's brilliant."},{"s":420.957,"e":422.357,"t":"And it's also..."},{"s":422.437,"e":423.637,"t":"a lot."},{"s":423.757,"e":427.547,"t":"It lands so much harder when you know who these people are, and what they've been"},{"s":427.597,"e":429.947,"t":"through. So don't start there."},{"s":429.997,"e":431.957,"t":"Save it. It'll be waiting."},{"s":432.377,"e":434.567,"t":"And here's my actual advice."},{"s":434.617,"e":436.087,"t":"Shop like a kid."},{"s":436.137,"e":438.727,"t":"When you were 10, you didn't need a reading order."},{"s":438.777,"e":442.007,"t":"You grabbed whatever cover looked cool, and figured it out."},{"s":442.057,"e":443.687,"t":"Find a character you like."},{"s":443.737,"e":445.567,"t":"For me, it was Colossus..."},{"s":445.617,"e":447.207,"t":"and I didn't even pick him."},{"s":447.257,"e":449.127,"t":"For you, it might be Storm."},{"s":449.177,"e":450.647,"t":"Then you can follow them."},{"s":450.697,"e":451.847,"t":"Read their stories."},{"s":451.897,"e":453.927,"t":"Jump around. Get confused."},{"s":453.977,"e":455.047,"t":"Look stuff up."},{"s":455.097,"e":456.657,"t":"That's half the fun."},{"s":457.081,"e":462.071,"t":"Quick note. I built ComixCatalog because I wanted one place to track what I own, and"},{"s":462.121,"e":463.271,"t":"what I'm hunting."},{"s":463.321,"e":467.471,"t":"You can search any of these books, see the covers, and throw the ones you want on a"},{"s":467.521,"e":471.511,"t":"wantlist, so you're not standing in a shop trying to remember issue numbers."},{"s":471.561,"e":472.791,"t":"It's free to use."},{"s":472.841,"e":473.921,"t":"Link's below."},{"s":474.34,"e":475.97,"t":"So, the shelf."},{"s":476.02,"e":477.25,"t":"Dark Phoenix."},{"s":477.3,"e":478.85,"t":"Days of Future Past."},{"s":478.9,"e":480.53,"t":"X-Cutioner's Song."},{"s":480.58,"e":482.61,"t":"God Loves, Man Kills."},{"s":482.66,"e":484.17,"t":"And House of M."},{"s":484.22,"e":487.73,"t":"And then House of X and Powers of X, when you're ready."},{"s":487.78,"e":490.21,"t":"Don't turn reading comics into homework."},{"s":490.26,"e":491.57,"t":"Go pick up a comic..."},{"s":491.62,"e":494.46,"t":"and come back and tell me which one you started with."}];
